# Backend (Spring Boot 4.1.1 / Java 21)

Packages: `catalog`, `commerce`, `identity`, `shared`. Controllers stay thin. Business rules live in application services, not `@RestController` and not `@Entity` getters with side effects.

Money: **`BigDecimal` only**. Parse CSV prices with `new BigDecimal(s)` after format checks; never `Double.parseDouble`.

## Transactions

- `@Transactional` on application services that write (checkout, import chunk, cart update).
- Checkout body has **no prices**. Snapshot `product.getPrice()` / `getName()` after the row lock. Fake pay uses server `order.total`.
- No `DELETE` mapping on orders. Shopper order GET filters by owner.
- Read-only queries: `@Transactional(readOnly = true)`.
- Do not `@Transactional` on controllers or repositories.

## Exceptions → HTTP

Map in `@RestControllerAdvice` to `{ "code", "message", "details" }`. Never return a stack trace.

| Situation | Type | Status |
|---|---|---|
| Signup created | — | 201 |
| Login / GET / PUT OK | — | 200 |
| Import accepted | — | 202 |
| Validation, empty cart | `ApiException` | 400 |
| No session | Security | 401 |
| SHOPPER hits `/api/admin/**` | Security | 403 |
| Unknown sku / job | `NotFoundException` | 404 |
| SKU exists, stock race, idempotency mismatch | domain | 409 |
| CSV too large | — | 413 |
| Unexpected | log + generic | 500 |

Do not use 200 for errors. Do not use 500 for “out of stock”. 3xx: SPA routes only (React Router), not the API.

```java
// ❌ BAD
return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of("error", e.getMessage()));

// ✅ GOOD
throw new InsufficientStockException(lines); // advice → 409
```

## OOP

- One use-case class per flow (`CheckoutService`, `CsvImportService`). Inject ports (repo, `PaymentClient`).
- Domain exceptions extend a shared `ApiException(code, status)`.
- JPA entities: constraints match DB. Money = `BigDecimal`, never `double`. Products: `@Version` on `version`; stale admin PUT → 409.
- `spring.jpa.open-in-view=false`. No business in default methods of repositories.
